      "explanation": "<p>(A) Alkyl chloride reacts with H<sub>2</sub>/Pd-BaSO<sub>4</sub> and reduced to alkyl aldehyde. This is known as Rosenmund reduction.</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wna4ab/bc1f3886-70a8-40ee-b0ed-c94810f2111e/643fb830-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wna4ac.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wna4ab/bc1f3886-70a8-40ee-b0ed-c94810f2111e/643fb830-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wna4ac.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 193 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wna4ab/bc1f3886-70a8-40ee-b0ed-c94810f2111e/643fb830-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wna4ac.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wna4ab/bc1f3886-70a8-40ee-b0ed-c94810f2111e/643fb830-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wna4ac.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wna4ab/bc1f3886-70a8-40ee-b0ed-c94810f2111e/643fb830-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wna4ac.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wna4ab/bc1f3886-70a8-40ee-b0ed-c94810f2111e/643fb830-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wna4ac.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wna4ab/bc1f3886-70a8-40ee-b0ed-c94810f2111e/643fb830-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wna4ac.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3wna4ab/bc1f3886-70a8-40ee-b0ed-c94810f2111e/643fb830-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wna4ac.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>(B) Carboxylic acid reacts with Cl<sub>2</sub>/P in aqueous medium to form 2-chlorocarboxylic acid. This reaction is known as HVZ reaction.</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnao1w/3388fc51-5f8d-4ea0-ac9e-c8daadea8710/73849040-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnao1x.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wnao1w/3388fc51-5f8d-4ea0-ac9e-c8daadea8710/73849040-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnao1x.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 193 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wnao1w/3388fc51-5f8d-4ea0-ac9e-c8daadea8710/73849040-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnao1x.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wnao1w/3388fc51-5f8d-4ea0-ac9e-c8daadea8710/73849040-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnao1x.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnao1w/3388fc51-5f8d-4ea0-ac9e-c8daadea8710/73849040-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnao1x.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wnao1w/3388fc51-5f8d-4ea0-ac9e-c8daadea8710/73849040-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnao1x.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wnao1w/3388fc51-5f8d-4ea0-ac9e-c8daadea8710/73849040-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnao1x.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3wnao1w/3388fc51-5f8d-4ea0-ac9e-c8daadea8710/73849040-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnao1x.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>(C) Alkyl amide reacts with Br<sub>2</sub> in presence of NaOH to give alkyl amine. This reaction is known as Hofmann bromide reaction,</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnb5mh/c7c0a23a-5f7d-477d-bde4-5771af00c817/811799a0-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d